From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Route screen-reader actions to DOM events

AccessKit's action requests were dropped (`ActionRequested` was a TODO),
so a screen reader could read the page but not use it. Nodes now say
what can be done with them (focus, click, scroll into view, expand or
collapse, increment and decrement), and the shell turns a request into a
new `UiEvent::Accessibility`, which the event driver does as the user's
own input would:

- Focus moves the focus, with focus and blur events;
- Click (and Expand and Collapse) focuses the element, as a browser does,
  then dispatches a click event, so handlers and default actions run;
- ScrollIntoView scrolls the element into view;
- Increment and Decrement focus a slider or spin button and press its
  up or down arrow key.

A click that has no default action used to clear the focus; it now keeps
it when the click lands in the focused element, so activating a focused
button doesn't lose the focus.
